  "title": "Subnet News — August 21, 2026",
  "summary": "Only 32% of tracked alpha markets rose as KubeTEE led the tape and Hippius fell hardest. BASE promoted Verda BYOK support, Cascade pinned its coordinated v0.6.0 worker rollout, UR published a 1.0 testnet release, and scoring or validator-integrity changes landed across Capcomp, AdTAO, Lium, BitMind, OpenRoboto, and Ditto.",
  "publishedAt": "2026-08-21T10:00:00-04:00",
  "coverageStart": "2026-08-20T10:00:00-04:00",
  "coverageEnd": "2026-08-21T10:00:00-04:00",
  "highlights": [
    {
      "headline": "Market breadth stays weak at 32% while KubeTEE gains 14.0%",
      "summary": "A block-8,893,644 snapshot taken five minutes before cutoff showed 32% of comparable subnet markets higher over the fixed window. SN90 KubeTEE led at about +14.0%, followed by Bitsec.ai and Minos; Hippius was the largest decliner at about -12.3%. These are alpha/TAO moves from fixed chain snapshots, not USD returns.",
      "importance": "high",
      "status": "verified",
      "sources": [
        {
          "label": "August 20 cutoff snapshot",
          "url": "https://github.com/buckZz7/dtao-trader/commit/b04e7158aca6847f4a2f066d2fb45fe50688ee87"
        },
        {
          "label": "August 21 cutoff snapshot",
          "url": "https://github.com/buckZz7/dtao-trader/commit/766af428f55f0acb45ef4a75b97024a9ac416fe1"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "headline": "BASE puts Verda bring-your-own-key capacity into production",
      "summary": "BASE added Verda BYOK as a mineable provider alongside Lium and then promoted the resulting image set to production before cutoff. The repository proves the code and production pin promotion; it does not independently prove how much Verda capacity was used during the window.",
